+# Cancelling a Booked Visit Stays Out of Scope
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+NG-5 read "changing or cancelling a visit once booked" and was confirmed deliberate on 2026-08-08 — see [Deleting Records and Amending Booked Visits Are Deliberately Out of Scope](2026-08-08-non-goal-deletion-and-visit-amendment.md). That ADR set the condition for reopening the row: an explicit owner decision recorded at intake, never the request itself.
+
+The owner recorded that decision on 2026-08-15: "Non-goal NG-5 is narrowed: cancelling a booked visit stays out of scope, but correcting its date and description is now in. Record the narrowing the way the project records non-goal changes."
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Keep NG-5 whole.** Rejected: the owner has decided otherwise, in the recorded form the earlier ADR requires.
+2. **Withdraw NG-5 entirely,** opening cancellation with correction. Rejected: the decision narrows the row, and it names cancellation as still out. A withdrawal would read consent into silence.
+3. **Narrow NG-5 to cancellation alone** (chosen).
+
+## Decision
+
+NG-5 now declines cancelling a booked visit and nothing else. Correcting a booked visit's date and description is a requirement, `REQ-VISITEDIT-001`.
+
+The sample still keeps no lifecycle state on a visit: there is no cancelled visit, and NG-4 keeps deletion out. Correction is forward correction, the same shape the owner and pet records already have.
+
+Reopening the cancellation half needs its own recorded owner decision, on the same terms the 2026-08-08 ADR set.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- The visit joins the owner and pet records as a correctable record; the sample now demonstrates that pattern on three entities rather than two.
+- A visit whose date has already passed cannot be saved unchanged, because the correction is held to the booking date rule. The consequence is recorded as an edge case, and whether it is intended is an open question.
+- NG-4 is untouched. The 2026-08-08 ADR stands for deletion and for the provenance of both rows.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-5
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the narrowed row.
+- [PRD Visit corrections](../prd.md#req-visitedit-001) — the requirement the narrowing admits.
