+### Visit corrections
+
+<a id="req-visitedit-001"></a>
+
+A booked visit can be corrected afterwards. Whoever opens a visit's correction form sees the date and the description currently recorded for that visit `[REQ-VISITEDIT-001]`. A correction is held to the same rules as booking: a description is required, and the date must be later than today. An accepted correction changes that visit in place, leaving the pet with the visits it already had, and the owner's record is shown again. A refused correction comes back as the form with the offending field named. Cancelling a booked visit stays out of scope (NG-5).
+
+**Done when:**
+- `[REQ-VISITEDIT-001]` given a booked visit, when its correction form is opened, then the form shows that visit's recorded date and description.
+- `[REQ-VISITEDIT-001]` given a booked visit, when a description and a future date are submitted, then that visit carries the new date and description, and the owner's record is shown.
+- `[REQ-VISITEDIT-001]` given a pet with one booked visit, when a correction is accepted, then the pet still has one visit.
+- `[REQ-VISITEDIT-001]` given a blank description, when the correction is submitted, then it is refused, the form is shown again, and the description is named.
+- `[REQ-VISITEDIT-001]` given a date of today or earlier, when the correction is submitted, then it is refused, the form is shown again, and the date is named.
+
+**Edge cases:**
+1. A visit whose date has already passed cannot be saved unchanged: a correction is held to the booking date rule.
+2. The owner's record carries no link to the correction form in this round; the form is opened directly.
+
+**ADR:** [ADR: Cancelling a Booked Visit Stays Out of Scope](adr/2026-08-15-non-goal-visit-cancellation.md)
+
